# <%= className %> REST API

Location: `apps/<%= fileName %>`. Stock NestJS HTTP application (`nest new` defaults).

## Layout

- `src/main.ts` — HTTP bootstrap (`PORT` env, default 3000).
- `src/app.module.ts` — root module; register feature modules here.
- `src/app.controller.ts` / `src/app.service.ts` — the sample route + logic.

## Adding a resource

Use the Nest CLI from inside the project:

```bash
cd apps/<%= fileName %>
nest g resource <name> --no-spec=false
```

That generates a module, controller, service, DTOs, and entity stub. Then import
the module in `app.module.ts` if the CLI didn't. Keep controllers thin — validation
via `class-validator` DTOs + a global `ValidationPipe`, logic in services.

## Running

```bash
nx serve <%= fileName %>      # nest start --watch
nx build <%= fileName %>
nx test <%= fileName %>
```

Deps are not installed by the generator — run `npm install` in `apps/<%= fileName %>` first.
